From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:03:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: no log file unless --debugfile asks for one

The game wrote logs/WZlog-MMDD_HHMMSS.txt in its Choices on every run,
and never removed them. On RISC OS it now only logs to a file given with
--debugfile, which !Run passes when Warzone2100$Log is set (along with
the stdout/stderr log). Other platforms keep upstream's behaviour.
---
 src/main.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
index 96a915f..04f9ba9 100644
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -1118,7 +1118,14 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 	make_dir(MultiPlayersPath, "multiplay", "players");
 	sstrcpy(MultiCustomMapsPath, "maps");
 
+#if defined(WZ_OS_RISCOS)
+	// No log file unless --debugfile names one (!Run passes it when
+	// Warzone2100$Log is set): a release shouldn't leave a file behind
+	// every time it runs.
+	if (false)
+#else
 	if (!customDebugfile)
+#endif
 	{
 		// there was no custom debug file specified  (--debug-file=blah)
 		// so we use our write directory to store our logs.
